description: Testing philosophy and RSpec conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

## Testing Philosophy

- Specs define behavior, not implementation
- Failing specs indicate either:
  - A bug
  - Or unclear requirements

---

## Domain Specs

- Test behavior, not internals
- No stubbing of domain methods
- Deterministic expectations

---

## Repository Specs

- Stub domain execution
- Use real ActiveRecord models
- Assert transactional behavior
- Assert persistence side effects

---

## What to Stub vs Real

| Layer      | Stub  | Real  |
|------------|-------|-------|
| Domain     | ❌    | ✅    |
| Repository | Domain| AR    |
| Controllers| Repository | ❌ |

---

## Anti-patterns

- Over-mocking
- Testing private methods
- Testing Rails internals
- Letting specs "pass by coincidence"

---

## Pending Specs

- Pending specs represent future behavior
- DO NOT remove them
- DO NOT implement beyond MVP unless instructed
